# dyn.md D-117 "Bound use through a register" (the analysis, WP-119):
# abseil's absl/time/format.cc twins of record WP-110 §G.1 (GCC 14 -O2),
# reduced to `FormatTime(Time, TimeZone)`. The -fPIE object names the
# exported `RFC3339_full` as `.rodata` anchor + 32 (`add x1, x5, 32`),
# past the two local strings before it; no relocation names it, so only
# the analysis finds the use, and mortar refuses it. The -fPIC twin
# loads its address from the GOT: every linker links it.
#@ spec: dyn.md "D-117"
#@ arch: aarch64
#@ xfail(mortar): M4: WP-123 (the D-117 analysis joined to the -shared link of WP-117)

as format-pie.s -o format-pie.o
as format-pic.s -o format-pic.o
link gcc -shared format-pic.o -Wl,-soname,libpic.so -o libpic.so
check readelf -rW libpic.so
  has: R_AARCH64_GLOB_DAT * _ZN4absl12lts_2024072212RFC3339_fullE
link(mortar) gcc -shared format-pie.o -Wl,-soname,libpie.so -o libpie.so
  exit: fail
  diag: relocation R_AARCH64_ADD_ABS_LO12_NC against symbol `*RFC3339_full*' which may bind externally can not be used when making a shared object
  diag: >>> the address .rodata+0x20 is computed by the instruction at *FormatTime*+0xc

